Your memories stay on your own computer, or on a KnowItAll2 server you run
and choose to connect. When you turn learning on, each learning call sends
a redacted excerpt of a finished session to your own Claude Code or Codex
account, as described in docs/testing.md. "Ask an agent to find these out"
in the app is different: it runs only when you press it, even with learning
off, and sends one agent on that account to read a project's files itself,
so nothing it reads is redacted first. On Claude Code 2.1 or later that
agent cannot read outside the project folder; on an older Claude Code, or
on Codex, whose read-only sandbox allows it, it can.
